license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - numa
  - lock-free
  - mpmc-queue
  - concurrent-data-structures
  - cache-conscious
  - work-stealing
  - cpp20
abstract: >-
  A cache-conscious, topology-aware multi-producer multi-consumer (MPMC)
  queue for high-core NUMA server CPUs. Gives each NUMA node its own
  bounded ring buffer, routes producers and consumers to their own node's
  ring, and moves work between nodes in batches instead of item by item.
preferred-citation:
  type: unpublished
  title: >-
    NumaRing: Topology-Aware Routing for NUMA-Local MPMC Queues, and What
    Broke When We Optimized It
  authors:
    - family-names: Sinha
      given-names: Parth Kumar
      orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-3120-9301"
      affiliation: "Independent Researcher, Oxford, United Kingdom"
  year: 2026
